================================================================================================================
soterm.py -- RULING 8(b) STEP ONE: THE CORPUS'S SPIN-ORBIT FORMS AGAINST THE STORE'S SIX INTERVALS
================================================================================================================

  so94's primary form is what fieldresidue.py uses.  The corpus holds two more -- so94's own declared exchange
  sensitivity, and so97's Koelling-Harmon form from a later session -- and never scored either against this
  store.  so97 differs from so94 in TWO ways at once (the potential and the mass factor), so both are varied
  separately here.  Every zeta is in cm-1; the ratio is to the store's measured interval.

  row    el    measured        loc       locX        dir      khloc         kh
  3p     Al        74.7       68.0       66.7       67.9       67.5       67.4
  4p     Ga       550.8      503.4      499.9      503.4      480.6      480.5
  5p     In      1475.1     1408.6     1402.8     1408.5     1246.1     1246.0
  6p     Tl      5195.1     5583.0     5570.9     5583.0     3918.0     3918.0
  4d     Y        212.1      262.4      258.0      262.2      259.9      259.7
  5d     La       421.3      572.9      567.5      572.8      558.3      558.1

  row    el  ratio to measured        loc       locX        dir      khloc         kh
  3p     Al                  0.910      0.893      0.908      0.903      0.902
  4p     Ga                  0.914      0.908      0.914      0.873      0.872
  5p     In                  0.955      0.951      0.955      0.845      0.845
  6p     Tl                  1.075      1.072      1.075      0.754      0.754
  4d     Y                   1.237      1.216      1.236      1.225      1.224
  5d     La                  1.360      1.347      1.360      1.325      1.325

  what each form is:
    loc    so94 primary        V_loc, M = 1
    locX   so94 sensitivity    V_loc + X/P, M = 1
    dir    the potential alone V_dir, M = 1
    khloc  the KH factor alone V_loc, M = KH
    kh     so97 verbatim       V_dir, M = KH

  <1/r^3> on the same normalised orbital (a0^-3), which is what an ORBITAL error moves and a form
  error does not:
    3p     Al        1.0799   eps -0.20959
    4p     Ga        3.0307   eps -0.20714
    5p     In        5.1856   eps -0.19458
    6p     Tl       12.1446   eps -0.18472
    4d     Y         1.6093   eps -0.23150
    5d     La        2.1428   eps -0.23566

  AND THE SAME FORMS ON THE CORRELATED ORBITAL -- the field the object takes its REMOVAL
  ENERGIES on (HF + form S with the PZ orbital SIC).  The potential in zeta stays electrostatic;
  what changes is the radial function.  If the fault is the orbital, it moves here.

  row    el    measured    zeta HF  zeta corr  ratio HF ratio corr    <1/r3> HF <1/r3> corr    move
  3p     Al        74.7       68.0       72.8     0.910      0.974       1.0799      1.1551  +6.97 %
  4p     Ga       550.8      503.4      548.1     0.914      0.995       3.0307      3.2981  +8.82 %
  5p     In      1475.1     1408.6     1544.4     0.955      1.047       5.1856      5.6844  +9.62 %
  6p     Tl      5195.1     5583.0     6200.3     1.075      1.193      12.1446     13.4860 +11.05 %
  4d     Y        212.1      262.4      271.8     1.237      1.281       1.6093      1.6650  +3.46 %
  5d     La       421.3      572.9      591.6     1.360      1.404       2.1428      2.2119  +3.22 %

  WHAT AN EXACTLY CORRECT SPIN-ORBIT TERM COSTS THE OBJECT
  The store measures zeta at all six anchored openings, so the object is re-read with the MEASURED
  zeta in place of the computed one.  That is a substitution of measurement for computation, the same
  act as gating on the store's measured removal limits, which the object already does.

  row    el   residual now  with measured zeta       move  | zeta on the corr orbital
  3p     Al       +0.00050            +0.00053    +0.031 mHa                    +0.00052
  4p     Ga       +0.00052            +0.00074    +0.216 mHa                    +0.00072
  5p     In       +0.00052            +0.00082    +0.303 mHa                    +0.00114
  6p     Tl       -0.00174            -0.00351    -1.767 mHa                    +0.00107
  4d     Y        -0.00381            -0.00416    -0.344 mHa                    -0.00375
  5d     La       -0.00290            -0.00394    -1.036 mHa                    -0.00277

  worst |residual|   now 0.00381   exact zeta 0.00416   zeta on the correlated orbital 0.00375 Ha
  RMS |residual|     now 0.00211   exact zeta 0.00279   zeta on the correlated orbital 0.00204 Ha

  ALL THREE ARE THE SAME OBJECT TO WITHIN THE SPREAD.  zeta itself moves 3-11 % between the
  uncorrelated and correlated orbitals and up to 36 % between computed and measured, but it reaches
  the removal energy only through the Lande term, which is small: the worst row moves 1.8 mHa and
  the RMS moves 0.07 mHa.  So the choice of orbital for zeta is NOT decided by the six rows -- the
  present one is kept because it is the record's, not because measurement prefers it -- and every
  variant sits inside the record's single-entrant class bound of 0.009 Ha
  (FINDING-HFTERM-SESSION-27).  NO CONCLUSION OF THIS PASS TURNS ON THE ZETA ERROR.

  PROTACTINIUM, where the store measures no interval and the computed zeta is all there is.
  The six measured rows bracket the error at 0.91 (3p) to 1.36 (5d), so the 5f figure is re-read
  with zeta scaled across that whole range:

    zeta scaled by   removal (eV)     t(5f)  move from 1.000
            1.0000          6.948    2.6359          +0.000 eV
            0.7353          6.935    2.6349          -0.014 eV
            0.8084          6.939    2.6352          -0.010 eV
            1.0989          6.953    2.6362          +0.005 eV
            1.0471          6.951    2.6361          +0.002 eV

  Across the ENTIRE range the six measured rows allow, the 5f removal energy moves by under
  0.02 eV -- against the +-0.11 eV typical bound the sibling ladder already carries.  The
  spin-orbit term is not what limits the 5f figure.
================================================================================================================
